    <node id="Indoor Environment">
      <data key="d0">Indoor Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"A space that is enclosed and used for various activities"&lt;SEP&gt;The Indoor Environment refers to a versatile enclosed space that blends living and functional areas, often resembling a living room. Characterized by wooden flooring, it is furnished with a variety of furniture and decor items, creating a welcoming atmosphere. This space is designed to accommodate various activities, making it both practical and comfortable for its occupants. Overall, the Indoor Environment combines aesthetic elements with functionality, embodying a harmonious living space.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">An indoor environment which may include various furniture pieces and objects, designed for comfort and functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indoor Environment is characterized as a contextual setting designed for specific tasks, featuring a living room-like setup that comprises various furniture and objects relevant to those tasks. Key elements within this indoor environment include a brown armchair, a dark gray spherical object, a small side table, and a robot arm, all of which contribute to its overall ambiance and functionality. This environment is not only arranged for comfort but also includes distinct areas dedicated to different functions, allowing for a seamless navigation of tasks. Moreover, the functional spaces and elements within the indoor environment provide a supportive context for activities, such as those involving a screwdriver and a sofa, thereby reinforcing its significance as a space tailored for interaction and engagement.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-cea350cefdc642e2d44bcc81397b05d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0d8e5fb4310903f4c2231b266aa6d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12f8717b377b7c2a7ebfe09e99c2a221</data>
