    <node id="Spatula">
      <data key="d0">Spatula</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">"A kitchen utensil used for flipping or spreading food."&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is a versatile and essential kitchen utensil used primarily for flipping, scraping, lifting, moving, mixing, serving, and spreading a variety of foods. Typically featuring a long handle and a flat, wide head, spatulas are commonly made from materials such as plastic or metal, with black being a prevalent color choice among dark composites. This indispensable tool holds great significance in both professional and home kitchens, enhancing efficiency in culinary activities.

When not in use, spatulas are often placed diagonally on countertops for easy access. Their design and functionality make them a crucial component in facilitating effective food handling and serving, thereby solidifying the spatula's important role in food preparation and presentation tasks.</data>
