      <data key="d2">"Items that are involved in the task execution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The significant items involved in the action or task being discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;The key objects interacted with are defined as specific items that play a significant role in the execution of a task. These objects can be categorized as those that are either directly involved in or affected by actions taken during the task. They also encompass items that are considered or intended for interaction by the agent, indicating their relevance in the task context. Furthermore, these objects are the ones that the embodied agent engaged with during the observation process, underscoring their active participation in the task execution. Overall, these key objects serve as crucial components throughout the task, facilitating actions and interactions necessary for successful completion.</data>
