    <node id="Living Room">
      <data key="d0">Living Room</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A room within a home designed for social interaction and relaxation."&lt;SEP&gt;The Living Room is a central domestic area in a house that is primarily designed for relaxation and socializing. It serves as a common space where family members and visitors can unwind, engage in leisure activities, and enjoy each other's company. This cozy and inviting area is typically furnished with comfortable seating arrangements and other items that enhance its multifunctional role. By emphasizing comfort and connection, the Living Room becomes the focal point for various gatherings and events, playing an essential role in facilitating social interaction and providing a space for relaxation within the home. It is a dedicated room designed specifically for both entertainment and social activities, making it an integral part of home life.&lt;SEP&gt;"An indoor space typically furnished for relaxation and entertainment"</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be used for watching TV;"N/A";"used_for_sitting;relaxation";sitting;social_interaction;socializing."</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"must_maintain_cleanliness;not_a_workspace"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The Living Room is a central area in a home designed for leisure and relaxation. It typically contains essential furniture such as a TV stand, television, and chairs, creating a functional and comfortable space. The atmosphere is enhanced by textures like wooden floors and a rug, which contribute to its inviting nature. In an organized layout, the couch is centrally located, with an armchair positioned on the left, promoting comfort and fostering social interaction among occupants.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Living Room is a cozy and inviting indoor space designed to facilitate social interaction, relaxation, and entertainment. It is characterized by a diverse array of furnishings and decor that enhance both its functionality and atmosphere. Key elements include a grey couch, a brown armchair, and a total of two armchairs, alongside a blue table, a geometric patterned rug, a plant, and a cabinet. Additional items, such as a pear on the couch and a ball, further contribute to the ambiance of this essential area.

As a crucial hub for gathering and leisure, the Living Room provides an environment conducive to interaction and unwinding. It plays a significant role in daily activities, particularly in helping individuals navigate the house, for instance, as the starting point for accessing the refrigerator. This spatial context has also been utilized for practical tasks, such as retrieving an orange and closing the refrigerator, showcasing the Living Room's functional aspect alongside its welcoming atmosphere.

Overall, the Living Room effectively combines practicality with a warm ambiance, making it an integral part of home life where various tasks can be performed amidst its comfortable furnishings.&lt;SEP&gt;The living room is identified as the overall location of the task involving the spatula and receptacle on the counters.&lt;SEP&gt;The living room serves as the spatial context for the agent’s navigation and observation activities.</data>
