      <data key="d7">Perception update describes a critical phase in a task where an agent becomes aware of the location of specific items, such as the orange on the TV stand. It is an event that encapsulates the process of gathering and interpreting sensory data within the kitchen environment. This update is also associated with the recording of environmental observations pertinent to the task at hand. Additionally, it relates to the successful observation of the contents found in cabinet 5, further emphasizing the importance of accurate perception in task execution.</data>
