    <node id="Left Counter">
      <data key="d0">Left Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Left Counter is a significant piece of furniture located in kitchens, specifically on the left side. This horizontal wooden surface is designated for various culinary tasks and serves multiple functions. It provides a practical area for users to transfer and place items such as fruits, utensils, and other kitchenware, thereby enhancing organization and efficiency within the kitchen environment. Although currently described as an empty surface, the Left Counter is integral to the kitchen workspace, facilitating the smooth operation of essential kitchen tasks. It functions similarly to the right counter, although positioned oppositely, reinforcing its role as a key component of kitchen organization and functionality.</data>
