      <data key="d7">The Right Counter is a multifunctional area located in the kitchen, specifically positioned to the right of the couch in the adjacent living room. Constructed from wood, this counter is designed to enhance kitchen functionality and is equipped with a robotic arm that assists in handling various kitchen utensils. The Right Counter plays a crucial role in organizing utensils and other items within the home environment. Among the items that can be found on this counter are a spatula, a toy airplane, and an orange, although the visibility of the toy airplane and orange is currently obstructed. Additionally, the Right Counter serves as the starting point for moving the spatula, which is significant in the context of activities that occur in both the kitchen and the living area. Overall, the Right Counter is integral to the spatial organization and operational flow between the kitchen and living room settings.</data>
