    <node id="Failure Outcome">
      <data key="d0">Failure Outcome</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"The outcome indicating the task was unsuccessful."&lt;SEP&gt;Failure Outcome refers to an event type characterized by the unsuccessful completion of a specific task or objective. It indicates a lack of success in achieving a planned goal, resulting in an unsatisfactory end. This concept highlights scenarios where attempts to accomplish specific tasks, such as finding or retrieving items, are unsuccessful, emphasizing the inability to complete tasks as intended. For example, if the intended goal was to move an orange and that goal was not achieved, this would exemplify a failure outcome. Moreover, it also signifies the resulting state from the repeated failure to complete the task, underscoring the consequences of failing to meet specified goals. In summary, a failure outcome encapsulates the ramifications of an unsuccessful attempt at completing a task.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
