    <node id="Task Goal">
      <data key="d0">Task Goal</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"Objective related to the movement of items within an environment."&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Goal refers to a defined objective or purpose associated with an action or activity, serving as an aim to achieve during a task. It is characterized as a navigational objective that guides the actions taken by an agent, encompassing a comprehensive aim focused on achieving specific outcomes through the execution of particular actions. 

In the context of navigating a kitchen environment, the Task Goal specifically represents the intended aim of an embodied agent to reach a designated location, such as a chair, while engaging and interacting with the surrounding environment. A key aspect of the Task Goal involves locating an orange and successfully transporting it to a predetermined destination, which necessitates navigating to the refrigerator, exploring its contents, and managing the items within. This process underscores the importance of exploration and interaction during task execution.

Moreover, the responsibilities related to the Task Goal include closing the refrigerator door after completing the action, indicating that multiple objectives are integrated into this cohesive framework. Overall, the Task Goal encapsulates various facets—reaching a specific location, engaging with the kitchen environment, transporting an item (specifically an orange), and managing the refrigerator door—into a unified objective aimed at fulfilling clearly defined outcomes. Additionally, it includes the objective or aim of moving other items, such as a spatula, further illustrating the multifaceted nature of the Task Goal within the operational context of the kitchen.</data>
