      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Task Goal defines the overarching purpose behind the actions of an embodied agent within a kitchen environment. It specifically aims to move objects from one location to another and also to navigate towards various points of interest, such as the refrigerator. A primary objective comprises locating an orange on the TV stand and transferring it to the sink, alongside retrieving a pear to transport to the sofa. This demonstrates the diverse nature of the tasks that guide the agent's behavior.

In addition to these primary tasks, the Task Goal includes the responsibility of checking the contents of the refrigerator and ensuring that its door is closed if left open, underscoring the importance of environmental observation in the agent's duties. The agent must also pick up a toy airplane from the right counter, adding further complexity to its set of objectives.

Moreover, additional responsibilities outline the importance of observing the kitchen environment from the right drawer of the counter and navigating to a chair, illustrating the multifaceted nature of the Task Goal. Overall, the Task Goal articulates a clear and comprehensive purpose for the agent’s actions within the kitchen, emphasizing the significance of monitoring the environment while performing specific tasks and preparing for interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Goal refers to the objective of moving one of the pear items to the designated sofa in the indoor environment.</data>
