    <node id="Hammer">
      <data key="d0">Hammer</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">The hammer is a widely utilized hand tool essential for various construction and repair tasks. It is designed with a medium-brown or light brown wooden handle, which is crafted for durability and comfort during use. The hammer features a heavy metallic head, typically appearing in shades of gray, silver, or even golden for aesthetic purposes. 

This versatile tool excels in driving nails, fitting parts, and breaking objects, making it indispensable for both professionals and DIY enthusiasts. It is often equipped with a flat striking surface that allows for efficient force application when driving nails into different materials. Many hammers also feature a claw design, enabling the easy removal of nails and enhancing their overall functionality.

The hammer's thoughtful construction ensures it remains a fundamental component of any toolkit, often found lying idle on a countertop, symbolizing its integral role in everyday manual tasks. Described as a light brown and gray tool, it is commonly depicted lying flat and ready for use, making it an iconic representation of manual labor.</data>
