    <node id="Action Results">
      <data key="d0">Action Results</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;Action Results refer to the outcomes that indicate the success or failure of attempted actions. They encompass the consequences of actions taken during a task, which can include both positive and negative results. The term signifies the various effects that arise from executing a task or action, ultimately reflecting the effectiveness of those actions in achieving desired objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Action Results indicate the outcomes of the actions taken, such as the ongoing observation status of the agent.&lt;SEP&gt;The Action Results provide a comprehensive overview of the achievements and status of entities following task execution. They summarize both successes and failures encountered during the process. Specifically, the Action Results indicate that there was a failure in the task execution due to the absence of a required plate. Additionally, the results detail a failed attempt to grasp a banana, contrasting this with the successful grasping and placement of a pear on the sofa. Overall, the Action Results encapsulate the mixed outcomes of the task, emphasizing the critical role of the required plate in the successful completion of the objectives.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-177fe53d62cd8f8a4738a850efb9bf13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf1504e51a4189248aa38fd2ee3413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74343abbe74fb662fca49366a4533755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4227f865845247f9e29eb245d9c49c9</data>
