    <node id="Uncertainty">
      <data key="d0">Uncertainty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"Lack of clarity or certainty regarding object locations."&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty refers to indications of doubt or a lack of clarity regarding objects or elements in the environment. It embodies the state of being unsure or having incomplete information about an object or task. This concept captures the presence of doubt and highlights the ambiguity surrounding specific aspects of a task, emphasizing the challenges that arise when information is insufficient or unclear.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The uncertainty regarding the locations of the toy airplane and orange contributed to the task failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty refers to the challenges encountered during a specific task, primarily involving the invisibility of the TV stand and the absence of nearby plates. This condition of uncertainty extends to the difficulty in identifying objects or elements present during navigation, which is further complicated by factors such as darkness and the hindrance posed by the TV stand's invisibility. Additionally, there is a lack of clarity regarding the exact location of the sink, which is not visible based on initial perceptions. Overall, the concept of uncertainty encapsulates the various obstacles faced in this scenario, particularly concerning visibility and object identification.</data>
