    <node id="pear">
      <data key="d0">pear</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">"A green, rounded fruit."&lt;SEP&gt;The pear is a medium-sized, green fruit characterized by its distinct pear shape, which is rounded at the base and tapers toward the top. It features a smooth texture and soft, edible flesh, indicating its ripeness. While primarily green, the pear can be considered small to medium-sized depending on the context. It is described as a spherical fruit commonly found on trees and is appreciated not only for its unique shape and flavor but also for its relevance in various tasks and discussions. The pear is recognized as a fresh fruit with distinct characteristics, making it enjoyed in culinary applications and beyond. Additionally, a specific instance notes a representation of a green, spherical pear placed to the lower left of a robotic arm.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"grasp;"observe;interact";move;place";transfer</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The entity "pear" is described in the context of its location, specifically noted as being positioned at the center-right of the counter. However, several descriptions are marked as "N/A," indicating a lack of additional information or context regarding the pear. As a result, the comprehensive description primarily emphasizes the pear's spatial placement without further elaboration.</data>
      <data key="d7">The pear is a significant green fruit observed in the kitchen environment, characterized by its smooth texture and rounded base. It plays an integral role in various home activities and has been documented in multiple locations throughout the house. Initially, the pear was moved from the kitchen counter to the sofa, then found on the living room couch, and later transferred to an allocated left counter. Currently, the pear resides within cabinet 5 on the left side of a hammer, resting on a flat dark surface, and is also noted to be situated to the lower left of a robotic arm in the countertop area. Occasionally, it is positioned on the left side of the kitchen counter, where it is described as fresh. Despite being the focal object during a task intended for relocation, this specific move was not executed successfully. Overall, the pear serves as a key object involved in various tasks and is consistently observed in different locations within the home environment, often adjacent to other objects.&lt;SEP&gt;The pear is located on the left side of the hammer within cabinet 5.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-e8fe7206d4da4b1264ec81ca9a6de819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4227f865845247f9e29eb245d9c49c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88d09cfcfcedc2adcc16d0314fe78275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd0f8cd733e3a8c8ba2e17fdc4e0b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1058b785568123c9dd67809d1e3c64cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4b6af94a6822cfe2dcbf1cfd9ea301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9649295b1c57c65b39ff8bcbd920173a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf9f4094ebfcd9a79a5e321661284a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d98281e318fd7984f676c6dcb97da97a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74343abbe74fb662fca49366a4533755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1a0c00327c58a2daa9dcadbc0296695</data>
