    <node id="TV Stand">
      <data key="d0">TV Stand</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A piece of furniture designed to hold electronic devices, such as a television."&lt;SEP&gt;"A piece of furniture used to hold electronic devices such as televisions"&lt;SEP&gt;The TV Stand is a specialized piece of furniture designed primarily to hold a television along with various other electronics and items. It typically features a rectangular shape and is characterized by its deep blue color. This particular TV Stand includes two cabinets with glass doors that showcase grid-like patterns, which enhance both its functionality and aesthetic appeal within a living space. By combining practicality with visual interest, it serves as a stylish and organized display for media and accessories, making it a suitable choice for modern interiors. Overall, the TV Stand is an essential piece of furniture for holding television sets and other media devices.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can support a TV;"N/A";"interact;"supports a TV;detect";hold other devices;navigate;provides a surface for objects";store items in the cabinets.";stores items</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"not_visible"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The TV Stand is an essential piece of furniture positioned centrally against the wall, providing support for a television mounted above it. It is prominently featured in the foreground of the living room setting, specifically located in front of a large flat-screen television.</data>
      <data key="d7">The TV Stand is a significant and multifunctional piece of furniture, primarily designed to support a television. It features a deep blue color and a rectangular shape, adorned with two cabinets that have distinct grid-like glass door patterns. This piece not only serves its primary role of holding a flat-screen TV—often mounted above it—but also enhances the functionality and aesthetic appeal of the living room.

Elevated slightly off the ground by short legs, the TV Stand provides a relevant flat surface that is central to the living room environment. It acts as a key destination for navigation and observation within the space. For instance, during specific tasks, such as the search for an orange, the TV Stand proved critical; the orange was initially not visible but was ultimately found on this stand. Furthermore, the TV Stand was also noted as the intended location for placing a plate, further emphasizing its multifunctional use in daily activities.

Overall, the TV Stand is both a practical and visually appealing component of the living room, contributing to the overall experience of the space while serving various purposes within daily life.&lt;SEP&gt;The TV stand is a flat surface where the observation took place, with various objects present around it.&lt;SEP&gt;The TV stand is the target location the embodied_agent navigates to for observation.</data>
