      <data key="d10">1772703441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="perception_update">
      <data key="d0">perception_update</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A "perception_update" refers to the process by which an agent recognizes and defines an object within its environment, significantly enhancing its awareness and understanding. This entity represents a crucial event class that facilitates the integration of new sensory information, allowing the agent to adjust its comprehension of tasks and surroundings as actions unfold. It signifies a shift or confirmation in the agent's understanding, reflecting modifications in perceptions based on observation or interaction with the environment. 

The "perception_update" encapsulates how sensory observations provide vital information about objects and tasks, showcasing the agent's adaptive response to sensory inputs. This event emphasizes the importance of continuous learning and adaptation in response to changing environmental stimuli, ultimately improving the agent's overall comprehension and interaction capabilities. In summary, a "perception_update" is an event type that communicates an update in perception, highlighting the dynamic nature of an agent's interactions with its environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"update"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The perception update represents an event type crucial for understanding an agent's navigation and interaction within its environment, particularly in the context of a kitchen setting. This event signifies a critical moment where the agent receives sensory or situational updates, enhancing its cognitive processes as it engages with its surroundings. For example, as the agent explores areas such as cabinet 5, it may notice changes or challenges related to visibility and access of expected objects, which can impact its ability to complete specific tasks.

The perception update captures the agent's ongoing cognitive experiences, allowing it to process visual and contextual information effectively. This process is essential for real-time adaptation, enabling the agent to adjust its understanding of the environment as it encounters scenarios where expected items, like an orange or a kitchen sink, are not visible. Such observations, while not directly triggering actions, play a significant role in refining the agent's recognition of its surroundings and the dynamics involved.

Additionally, the perception update encompasses lessons learned from past experiences, including failures during tasks, such as moving a spatula. These insights contribute to the agent's overall operational framework, emphasizing the importance of perception updates in enhancing its task performance and situational awareness. In summary, the perception update is integral to the embodied agent's ability to navigate and understand its environment effectively, reinforcing its cognitive functions during the execution of kitchen-related tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-44c7d4402d89e167772ed7b4de4c2e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef495c3da8ad2e873c7dd3f68549a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf1504e51a4189248aa38fd2ee3413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf9f4094ebfcd9a79a5e321661284a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e81386ebdc9a6d8f85d441f2f0278a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b875acc27aada74fbf5b8b08480ffe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84aaf0b30ba83e298b755bb648e6079e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7a3f830c9003a2fcb1b91e91ae47a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b53e4715d0fd6b6527a9cb079b06d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6878dc8cc7c3d9d8b574d4ab20c10418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1058b785568123c9dd67809d1e3c64cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e487c95a61038aa96df99ce4d9dd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2663373a7c15d583525613b528aaf782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3110c2c46307410294a70a5f9d323898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4227f865845247f9e29eb245d9c49c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d2c0d609132b708454a6e443bb635b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0c8dda21f0a7bd359abef42ad2fc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53daedf4d04d6753bedcb7a46e631c8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26187e3c991b49bfc7f789f4aafc93f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4f8a99c2c3feb883c8a2b6716e4e6e</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d10">1772703449</data>
    </node>
    <node id="action_execution">
      <data key="d0">action_execution</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Action execution refers to an event type that signifies the carrying out of specific tasks aimed at achieving defined goals. It involves the performance of anticipated actions, representing how agents navigate and interact with various objects in their environment to accomplish designated objectives. This process encompasses the implementation of planned activities by an agent, characterized by the systematic execution of tasks based on requests or perceptions.

Essential to translating theoretical plans into concrete outcomes, action execution relies on the agent’s ability to perceive and react to the surrounding context. The act not only involves executing assigned tasks but also requires careful observation and intentionality from the agent. Overall, action execution plays a vital role in the effective realization of tasks and goals, ensuring that plans are successfully implemented through deliberate and informed actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"perform"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Action execution refers to a specific event type encompassing the completion of tasks performed by an embodied agent, particularly in a kitchen environment. This intricate process highlights the agent's engagement in a comprehensive sequence of actions aimed at effectively manipulating various objects. A notable example of action execution involves the manipulation of a pear, where the agent navigates its surroundings and executes a series of attempts to grasp and transport the pear to a designated location, such as the left counter. This scenario illustrates both successful actions and repeated failures, shedding light on the complexities of the operational goals that the agent seeks to achieve.

In addition to the manipulation of the pear, action execution involves the agent's interactions with other items, such as an orange and a toy airplane. The agent makes attempts to grasp and move specific objects, exemplified by successfully transferring an orange from the TV stand to the sink while also confronting challenges, such as failed attempts to grasp a banana and additional efforts to manipulate the orange from the sink. Furthermore, action execution includes the attempts to move a spatula from one counter to another, which ultimately resulted in failure, emphasizing the agent's struggle with various kitchen tasks.

Overall, action execution encapsulates the multifaceted nature of the agent's work within the kitchen environment, illustrating the complex interplay between navigation, physical manipulation, and interaction with numerous kitchen objects. This concept underscores the challenges and successes encountered during operational activities and the anticipated implementation of these tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-84aaf0b30ba83e298b755bb648e6079e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c7d4402d89e167772ed7b4de4c2e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26187e3c991b49bfc7f789f4aafc93f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8fe7206d4da4b1264ec81ca9a6de819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d2c0d609132b708454a6e443bb635b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e487c95a61038aa96df99ce4d9dd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf9f4094ebfcd9a79a5e321661284a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74343abbe74fb662fca49366a4533755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b875acc27aada74fbf5b8b08480ffe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9649295b1c57c65b39ff8bcbd920173a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9a1e3929880811a0a5d3b7f0c6c5747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e81386ebdc9a6d8f85d441f2f0278a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf1504e51a4189248aa38fd2ee3413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3110c2c46307410294a70a5f9d323898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0c8dda21f0a7bd359abef42ad2fc5</data>
