      <data key="d0">Indoor Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"An enclosed area primarily used for various activities."&lt;SEP&gt;The Indoor Space is defined as a general indoor environment that showcases various objects and furniture, characterized by its enclosed nature, which typically includes walls and a roof. This structured setting facilitates a variety of activities and features a specific layout with tan flooring and walls, complemented by closed doors. The arrangement of furniture within the space indicates its design for particular functions, contributing to its overall character and purpose as a well-organized environment.&lt;SEP&gt;"Area designed for living or activities within a building."</data>
