      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The entity, Indoor Space, is characterized by a specific focus on interactions within a defined environment. It encompasses all interactions that occur in this space, which is typically delineated by walls and features closed doors. This description suggests that the Indoor Space is an enclosed area where activities can take place privately, although no additional details are provided regarding its purpose or design.</data>
      <data key="d7">An indoor space is the overarching setting that contains the sofa and the robotic arm, facilitating various interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Indoor Space is a defined environment suitable for various activities, specifically characterized by tan flooring and closed doors. This setting includes walls that create a static atmosphere with limited activity observed during observation. The space prominently features a sofa positioned against a beige wall, alongside various objects that contribute to the context of tasks carried out within it. One task involved the navigation of an orange within this indoor space, where visibility was hindered due to the presence of two closed doors and a robotic arm. Overall, the Indoor Space serves as the location for navigation and observation tasks, with a flat brown surface that includes a chair, enhancing the functional aspects of the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The task occurred in an indoor space with tan flooring.</data>
