    <node id="hammer">
      <data key="d0">hammer</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">The hammer is a versatile and essential tool commonly utilized in construction and woodworking. It features a metallic head, typically crafted from durable metal such as silver, and a wooden handle, which is usually light to medium-brown. The hammer is designed with a flat side for striking, as well as a claw for removing nails, enhancing its functionality for driving nails, fitting parts, and breaking objects. Its effective and simple design allows it to perform a wide range of manual tasks, showcasing its reliability and effectiveness in everyday use. Additionally, the hammer can be depicted as being placed diagonally or positioned next to objects, emphasizing its practical applications in various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"strike;"use;clamp";hit;hit";hold</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
