      <data key="d7">The hammer is an essential hand tool primarily located in the kitchen, recognized for its functional uses. It features a wooden handle, which shows slight wear, and a metallic head made of steel. This versatile tool is primarily used for pounding and pulling nails, highlighting its integral role in various kitchen tasks. Specifically, the hammer is positioned on the right side of the kitchen counter, adjacent to a pear, and also found on a flat dark surface in cabinet 5. Additionally, it is mentioned to be present among other stationary objects in the kitchen sink, although its exact usage in that context is not specified. Overall, the hammer's accessibility in the kitchen underscores its importance as a readily available tool for multiple functions.</data>
