      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Navigation Task is defined as a specific task that involves purposeful movement towards designated locations for the purpose of observation. This task entails navigating to specific points, such as the refrigerator, chair, TV stand, and sofa, all while maintaining an awareness of the surrounding environment. The emphasis is on the act of moving effectively to these objectives and being observant of the surroundings during this process. Thus, the Navigation Task encompasses both the act of navigating to specified locations and the intent to observe relevant objects and details in the vicinity.</data>
