      <data key="d7">The Navigation Task is a defined action that an embodied agent is required to execute within a kitchen environment. This task involves directing the agent to move towards specific locations, such as a chair, a sofa, or a refrigerator, primarily for observation purposes. When approaching these locations, the agent not only observes but may also engage with certain objects, such as interacting with the chair.

Specifically, the agent navigates towards the chair to both observe and interact, whereas the movement towards the refrigerator is characterized by observing the surroundings without any specific goals other than navigation itself. It is noted that during these navigation efforts to the refrigerator, the agent may encounter constraints due to the uncertain nature of its surroundings. Additionally, the task also includes navigating to the sofa solely for observation. Overall, the Navigation Task encapsulates the activities the agent undertakes in moving to designated locations within the kitchen, combining elements of observation and interaction under varying environmental conditions.</data>
