      <data key="d2">The spatula is a versatile kitchen tool commonly employed in various culinary tasks, including flipping, serving, mixing, and spreading food. Typically characterized as a durable black utensil, it is designed for efficiency during cooking processes. Constructed from materials suitable for food preparation, the spatula plays a crucial role in lifting and maneuvering ingredients, making it an essential item in any kitchen. Overall, it serves as a multifunctional object used for flipping, stirring, and serving a variety of foods.</data>
