      <data key="d2">"A surrounding or context in which activities and observations occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The surrounding space or context in which objects exist and are observed"&lt;SEP&gt;The environment is defined as the overall surroundings in which an embodied agent operates. It encompasses the surrounding context that influences actions and observations, as well as the physical conditions or context under which these actions take place. Additionally, it refers to the physical space where objects are situated, highlighting the interaction between the agent and its surroundings.</data>
