    <node id="spatial_context">
      <data key="d0">spatial_context</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Spatial context refers to the positional relations between objects and spaces, encompassing the arrangement and layout of various elements within an environment. It involves the spatial relationships of objects as they relate to one another during specific tasks, reflecting how those objects interact or are organized within a given area. Overall, spatial context provides an essential understanding of how objects and spaces are organized and relate to each other in a defined context.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The spatial_context provides a comprehensive overview of the position of the robotic arm in relation to a grey cabinet, emphasizing its position in the environment rather than solely focusing on target objects. It encompasses both global and local relationships, detailing how various objects are positioned in relation to one another. Specifically, the spatial_context identifies the location of the spatula on the right counter and the receptacle on the left counter. Overall, it presents important information about the physical relationships among objects within the observed environment.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-49e81386ebdc9a6d8f85d441f2f0278a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44c7d4402d89e167772ed7b4de4c2e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9a1e3929880811a0a5d3b7f0c6c5747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8fe7206d4da4b1264ec81ca9a6de819</data>
