      <data key="d7">The right counter holds the spatula and is part of the overall layout in the indoor living space.&lt;SEP&gt;The right counter is a surface located in the indoor living area that plays several roles in navigation and retrieval attempts. Initially, it was where the spatula was located. The right counter served as a significant location during navigation attempts; however, it did not function as the final destination for the pear. Additionally, it was the site from which the embodied agent attempted to retrieve a toy airplane and an orange, but these items were not accessible. The right counter was also identified as the target location for retrieving the toy airplane and orange, although these items were not visible in the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;The right counter serves as the starting point for the task but is associated with an expected spatula that was not located.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-9649295b1c57c65b39ff8bcbd920173a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e81386ebdc9a6d8f85d441f2f0278a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9a1e3929880811a0a5d3b7f0c6c5747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a5e48d2ff5b0e6cf0b9025d4ef04014</data>
