    <node id="failure_outcome">
      <data key="d0">failure_outcome</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "failure outcome" refers to a result that signifies the unsuccessful completion of a task. It encompasses events where an action does not meet its intended goal, leading to unsuccessful attempts, such as trying to pick up and transfer an object, like a pear, to a designated location, such as the left counter. Overall, a failure outcome indicates non-completion of a task and signifies a failure to achieve the desired goal.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"fail"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The failure outcome refers to the series of unsuccessful attempts made by an embodied agent to grasp different objects, including an orange, a pear, and a spatula. The descriptions indicate that the agent's attempts to grasp the orange were obstructed, preventing successful retrieval. Similarly, the efforts to interact with the pear did not result in achieving the intended goal, illustrating additional challenges faced by the agent during these attempts. Furthermore, the failure outcome highlights the agent's specific inability to pick up the spatula, particularly after navigating away from it. Collectively, these descriptions underscore the agent's overall failure to successfully retrieve the orange, pear, and spatula, signifying that the tasks aimed at retrieving these objects were ultimately not accomplished due to various obstructions and circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-a4d2c0d609132b708454a6e443bb635b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e487c95a61038aa96df99ce4d9dd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9649295b1c57c65b39ff8bcbd920173a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9a1e3929880811a0a5d3b7f0c6c5747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e81386ebdc9a6d8f85d441f2f0278a</data>
