    </node>
    <node id="kitchen sink">
      <data key="d0">kitchen sink</data>
      <data key="d1">receptacle</data>
      <data key="d2">The kitchen sink is a specially designed receptacle for washing dishes and food items, serving as a crucial component within a kitchen environment. Typically made from materials like stainless steel or porcelain, the kitchen sink facilitates various kitchen tasks, particularly those related to cleaning and food preparation. Acting as a central location for holding water, the kitchen sink meets the washing needs associated with household tasks, making it an essential fixture for any kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"fill;clean;clean";drain;use";wash"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The kitchen sink is situated below the countertop, specifically to the left of the stove, within the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d7">The kitchen sink is an essential fixture situated in the kitchen area, primarily designed for functional purposes related to washing. It is identified as a receptacle located below the countertop, often positioned to the left of the stove. This key kitchen element is commonly used for washing dishes and preparing food, serving as a site where various objects, including food items like oranges, can be found. The kitchen sink plays a critical role in facilitating various tasks within the kitchen environment, highlighting its importance in daily culinary activities.</data>
