      <data key="d2">"The modifications in the condition or status of objects throughout the task execution."&lt;SEP&gt;State Changes refer to the adjustments that occur after actions have taken place, reflecting alterations in the status of objects involved. This includes information regarding changes in status that result from the performance of specific actions, as well as results that indicate the movement of objects during a task. Additionally, State Changes encompass modifications in the status of the involved items both during and after the execution of a task.</data>
