      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">State Changes refer to the alteration of the conditions of various objects, including a pear, a sofa, and a robotic arm, during task execution. They highlight the processes involved, such as the pear being moved from the sofa to the left counter following the completion of a task. Additionally, State Changes indicate that an orange was transferred from the TV stand to the sink, and the sink now contains both the orange and a bottle of dish soap. Furthermore, State Changes encompass the movement of the pear from the kitchen counter to the sofa, while a banana remains on the kitchen counter throughout these activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The State Changes are described as N/A because no interaction with objects occurred.</data>
