    <node id="Objects">
      <data key="d0">Objects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Objects" serves as a general referent for items within a described scene. It includes general items present in an indoor environment, each capable of serving various functions. Specifically, it encompasses various items found in the kitchen that are used for cooking and food preparation. This comprehensive description highlights the versatile nature of the objects, emphasizing their role in both general indoor settings and the specific context of kitchen activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Objects refer to a collection of items analyzed in the text, encompassing various shapes, colors, and functionalities. They represent the various items described in the environment, including specific examples such as a brown armchair, a dark gray sphere, and a blue robot arm, which together shape the spatial dynamics of the setting. Additionally, the Objects category includes an array of items typically found in a kitchen, such as utensils, appliances, and ingredients used for culinary practices. Overall, the term 'objects' denotes various items that possess specific attributes and relationships within the described environment.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c373a33b7f40d867bb7889415b47e8ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12f8717b377b7c2a7ebfe09e99c2a221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191e598f72ba5bb9098d142aa877c30b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbbb4c723348e17ec00fda3f50df18c</data>
