    <node id="Sponge">
      <data key="d0">Sponge</data>
      <data key="d1">cleaning tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sponge is a cleaning tool typically made from absorbent material, known for its effectiveness in scrubbing surfaces. It is characterized as a soft, absorbent material that is specifically designed for cleaning purposes. One common type of sponge is described as a flat, pale yellow sponge, which highlights its typical appearance. Overall, sponges are essential tools in cleaning, blending functionality with versatility in various cleaning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"Used for scrubbing;"can absorb liquid;absorbing liquid";used for cleaning"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"on the counter above the orange cup"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The sponge is a cleaning tool commonly found on the counter above the orange cup, positioned flat on the counter surface. It is utilized primarily for cleaning tasks in the kitchen environment, where it serves to scrub surfaces effectively. The sponge is often used in conjunction with cleaning solutions to enhance its cleaning capabilities and to absorb spills, making it an essential item for maintaining cleanliness in the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-2b703e57f7f312079f6c2ad3c93d259e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7717aa9c0edd7bec036e22965a596b5</data>
