      <data key="d7">The interior of a refrigerator typically features a textured design with vertical grooves or ridges for aesthetic and functional purposes, maintaining a clean appearance with muted colors like off-white or light grey.&lt;SEP&gt;The refrigerator interior surface features a textured design with vertical grooves or ridges that serve aesthetic and functional purposes such as holding shelving units or guiding airflow. The color is often muted, like off-white or light grey, to maintain a clean appearance.</data>
