    <node id="navigation">
      <data key="d0">navigation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Navigation refers to the act or process of directing movement in space, which involves moving and selecting a path to a destination. It encompasses the process of moving from one place to another while observing the surroundings, as well as finding one’s way to a specific destination.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"move;observe"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Navigation encompasses purposeful movement aimed at reaching specific locations for observation or action. It involves the actions taken by an embodied agent to move to particular spaces, such as within a kitchen or towards specific objects. For instance, navigation includes the process of moving to the left drawer of a kitchen counter, as well as reaching for a chair. Overall, navigation is characterized by its goal-oriented nature in facilitating movement to designated areas or items.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-3110c2c46307410294a70a5f9d323898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4efe4535ba7fd9b92fec1ad1e7648658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b875acc27aada74fbf5b8b08480ffe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26187e3c991b49bfc7f789f4aafc93f5</data>
