    <node id="Navigation">
      <data key="d0">Navigation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Navigation refers to the act of moving from one location to another, encompassing the process of traversing through an environment in order to reach a specific destination. It involves orienting oneself within the environment and actively moving towards a designated location.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"move;"navigate";identify";locate</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Navigation is a fundamental action required by the embodied agent to complete assigned tasks in the kitchen. It encompasses various activities, including the agent's movement towards specific locations such as the TV stand, as outlined in the task's action sequence. Additionally, navigation involves directing the robotic arm to particular spots, notably cabinet 4, which is integral to the overall operation within the kitchen context. The process also includes moving through the environment to locate and access the refrigerator as part of the assigned tasks. Overall, navigation is a crucial component that facilitates the agent's ability to effectively interact with its surroundings and accomplish its objectives in the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-dbc9e5b1a99517c95fb6c76a1254a379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b12ac4b5e7ef4ee723211268193b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c75d39513265b557d4b3ba5fc81b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26ad68c6116f014d0032d19c0c00e620</data>
