    </node>
    <node id="observation">
      <data key="d0">observation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"The act of closely watching or monitoring something."&lt;SEP&gt;Observation is the act of carefully monitoring or watching something, which involves not only noticing or perceiving various elements but also examining the environment or specific items. It encompasses the careful observation of surroundings to gather information and gain insights.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"watch;analyze"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Observation refers to the action performed by an embodied agent to gather information about its surrounding environment at various locations. This includes the process of examining the contents of cabinet 5 upon reaching it, as well as the action taken after navigation to understand the environment better. Additionally, observation entails the focused engagement of the embodied agent with the environment and objects while at the table, as well as the actions undertaken after reaching the chair. Overall, observation encompasses the systematic efforts of the embodied agent to collect information in different settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Observation refers to the event where the embodied_agent engages with the kitchen environment and the objects present.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-1058b785568123c9dd67809d1e3c64cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb5f80c3116a93720e49290acef46cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b875acc27aada74fbf5b8b08480ffe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4efe4535ba7fd9b92fec1ad1e7648658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3110c2c46307410294a70a5f9d323898</data>
