    <edge source="Task Request" target="Action Execution">
      <data key="d11">118.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The Task Request initiates the Action Execution phase, engaging an embodied agent to perform various tasks as directed. This process involves the agent executing specific actions, such as moving objects like a pear and an orange, which are integral to completing the assigned tasks. Additionally, the agent is responsible for follow-through actions, notably closing the refrigerator door. The relationship between the Task Request and Action Execution is clear, as the action execution is a direct response to the task request. It encompasses not only the movements of the objects but also essential navigation and observation required for fulfilling the designated tasks. Overall, the agent demonstrates a comprehensive engagement in executing the instructions, successfully moving the pear to the sofa while ensuring that the refrigerator door is closed, thus achieving the desired outcome as prompted by the task request.&lt;SEP&gt;The task request initiates the action execution as part of completing the assigned task.</data>
