      <data key="d12">The Task Goal and Task Request are closely interrelated concepts within the context of task execution. The Task Request defines the objective of the task and outlines the specific goals that need to be accomplished. It is derived from the Task Goal, which, in this instance, includes the specific goal of closing the refrigerator door. Additionally, the Task Request provides detailed guidance on achieving the precise goal associated with the task involving the pear. Overall, the Task Request serves to articulate and clarify the objectives necessary for successful task completion.&lt;SEP&gt;The task request involves achieving the specified task goal of closing the refrigerator door.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Request is aimed at fulfilling the Task Goal of moving the spatula to the receptacle.</data>
      <data key="d13">goal setting,goal-directed action,goal-oriented,objective clarification,objective definition,objective-oriented,task direction,task initiation,task objective,task specification</data>
      <data key="d14">chunk-f141569c90d0dc3f466444b6898c4311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f0fdb089894fccdb13df2ba4e5c945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26ad68c6116f014d0032d19c0c00e620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9649295b1c57c65b39ff8bcbd920173a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0c8dda21f0a7bd359abef42ad2fc5</data>
