    </edge>
    <edge source="Task Request" target="Embodied Agent">
      <data key="d11">161.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The Embodied Agent is an active entity specifically designed to execute a variety of Task Requests primarily within a kitchen environment. Its main responsibilities include navigating to particular locations such as the refrigerator and the sink, while also ensuring that the refrigerator remains closed. Environmental awareness is a critical aspect of the agent's functionality, as it must observe its surroundings, particularly the kitchen countertop and cabinet, to effectively complete its tasks.

The agent's roles involve performing specific actions dictated by Task Requests, which may include moving items, such as transferring a pear from the kitchen counter to the sofa or finding and moving an orange. Moreover, the Embodied Agent is required to navigate to the refrigerator push point as part of its operational tasks, demonstrating its versatility and adaptability in managing a diverse array of responsibilities within the kitchen setting. Overall, the Embodied Agent effectively combines navigation, observation, and item handling to fulfill the various Task Requests it receives.</data>
      <data key="d13">action directive,action execution,action initiation,action involvement,actor involvement,actor role,agency,agent action,agent involvement,navigation,navigation task,observation,responsibility,task accomplishment,task engagement,task execution,task fulfillment,task initiation,task performance,task responsibility</data>
