    <edge source="Task Request" target="Perception Update">
      <data key="d11">89.0</data>
      <data key="d12">Task Request and Perception Update indicate two distinct types of events pertaining to task execution.&lt;SEP&gt;The entities, Task Request and Perception Update, are interconnected components within a defined operational framework that facilitate interaction with an observed environment. The Task Request delineates the specific action needed, which in this context, involves navigating to the refrigerator and potentially observing other relevant elements, such as the spatula's status. This process instigates a Perception Update, which reflects the outcomes of executing the Task Request. The Perception Update provides insights into the environment, capturing any changes in understanding or context that occur as a result of fulfilling the task related to the refrigerator. Consequently, the relationship between Task Request and Perception Update is such that the latter represents the consequences and insights gained from successfully addressing the former, highlighting the continuous loop of observation and understanding within this operational sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;The task request initiated a perception update to confirm the presence of objects intended for retrieval.</data>
