    <edge source="Perception Update" target="Embodied Agent">
      <data key="d11">106.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The Embodied Agent is engaged in a vital process known as a Perception Update, which is designed to enhance its understanding of the immediate kitchen environment. Throughout this process, the agent actively navigates various areas within the kitchen, including the sink, counter, and refrigerator, to observe the status of items and gather important data about its surroundings. This active engagement is crucial for developing a comprehensive understanding of the context in which the Embodied Agent operates.

However, the Embodied Agent faces certain limitations during the Perception Update, particularly when the environment lacks identifiable features, which can hinder its ability to gather complete information. Despite these challenges, the overarching goal of the Perception Update is clear: to equip the Embodied Agent with essential insights that facilitate its subsequent tasks effectively. This process not only involves general observations in the kitchen but also occurs after the agent reaches specific points, such as the refrigerator push point, further highlighting its role in constantly updating its perception of the kitchen environment.</data>
