    <edge source="Action Execution" target="Success Outcome">
      <data key="d11">96.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The Action Execution refers to the process of completing specific tasks that lead to desired outcomes. In this context, it is demonstrated through two distinct successful actions: closing the refrigerator door and placing a pear on the sofa. The successful execution of these actions led to positive success outcomes, reinforcing the effectiveness of the actions taken. Specifically, the closing of the refrigerator door marked the effective completion of that task, while the placement of the pear also contributed to the overall success. Therefore, the Action Execution not only resulted in multiple successful outcomes, showcasing the capability of achieving desired results through effective task performance, but it also indicated that all actions performed were executed correctly.</data>
      <data key="d13">achievement,execution success,goal completion,outcome success,positive result,result,success,successful execution,task achievement,task completion</data>
      <data key="d14">chunk-26ad68c6116f014d0032d19c0c00e620&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf9f4094ebfcd9a79a5e321661284a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8fe7206d4da4b1264ec81ca9a6de819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f141569c90d0dc3f466444b6898c4311</data>
