      <data key="d11">51.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The Embodied Agent is involved in a dual-focused activity that incorporates both observation and the achievement of a specific task goal. While initially described as engaged in observation without a clearly defined task, further details reveal that its engagement includes navigating to the refrigerator, which serves as a critical component of the overall task goal. The primary objective of the Embodied Agent is to retrieve an orange, and its actions are directed toward fulfilling this task goal. Therefore, the Embodied Agent's activities are not only centered on observing its environment but also on effectively achieving the task goal of retrieving the orange by navigating to the refrigerator. In summary, the Embodied Agent's purpose combines the goal of observing the environment with the practical task of retrieving an orange, all guided by the overarching task goal of navigating to the refrigerator push point.</data>
