    <edge source="Sink" target="Countertop">
      <data key="d11">67.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The countertop and sink are part of the kitchen’s work area, facilitating food preparation and cleaning tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The countertop is a functional piece of kitchen furniture that incorporates an integrated sink, establishing a significant structural relationship between the two entities. The sink, which is embedded within the countertop, is positioned lower than the countertop itself, demonstrating a thoughtful design that enhances the spatial arrangement and functionality of the kitchen area. As a component of the overall countertop setup, the sink serves as a dedicated space for washing and preparing items, emphasizing its essential role in the kitchen. Overall, the connection between the countertop and the sink illustrates an efficient integration that supports various cleaning and washing tasks, highlighting the design's focus on practicality and user convenience.</data>
