    <edge source="task_request" target="perception_update">
      <data key="d11">44.0</data>
      <data key="d12">Both task_request and perception_update represent events that influence how an embodied agent interacts with the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The entities "perception_update" and "task_request" are categorized as event types that signify specific actions undertaken by the embodied_agent in reaction to environmental cues. The task_request prompts the embodied_agent to initiate a certain action or task, while the subsequent perception_update delivers feedback regarding the performance of that task and provides information about the objects involved. The interplay between these two entities is evident, as the task_request leads to a perception_update, which in turn helps the agent assess the status of the objects related to the request. Overall, the relationship between perception_update and task_request is crucial for the embodied_agent to effectively respond to and navigate its environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The task_request culminates in a perception_update, where the outcomes of the observation are processed.</data>
      <data key="d13">action outcome,action response,event types,feedback; directive completion,information processing,interaction,objective completion,observation result,perception,task completion</data>
      <data key="d14">chunk-b4227f865845247f9e29eb245d9c49c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0c8dda21f0a7bd359abef42ad2fc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53daedf4d04d6753bedcb7a46e631c8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1058b785568123c9dd67809d1e3c64cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf9f4094ebfcd9a79a5e321661284a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4f8a99c2c3feb883c8a2b6716e4e6e</data>
      <data key="d15">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d16">ASSOCIATION</data>
      <data key="d17">1772703453</data>
    </edge>
