    <edge source="task_request" target="action_execution">
      <data key="d11">82.0</data>
      <data key="d12">The action_execution is a direct consequence of the task_request, which serves to outline the specific goals that must be achieved by the embodied agent. The task_request initiates the process, guiding the agent to attempt to complete the assigned tasks, which include detailed instructions such as fetching an item from the drawer. This involves the performance of specific actions to fulfill the request. The relationship between the task_request and action_execution is fundamental, as the former drives the latter, ensuring that all necessary actions are effectively executed during the retrieval process. For instance, the action execution occurs during the attempt to complete an orange move task, further illustrating the role of the task_request in leading to an actionable phase where the agent actively performs the necessary tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The task_request leads to the action_execution as it initiates the process of attempting to retrieve the specified objects.&lt;SEP&gt;The task request initiates the action execution of moving the spatula.</data>
      <data key="d13">action performance,cause-effect,execution,execution linkage,linked events,sequence of actions,task execution,task execution flow,task initiation,task interaction,task management,task progression,workflow</data>
